                <pb facs="0611" n="512" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg512"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/2828: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caldwell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-08-27T09:00:00+01:00">August 27, 1936—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 27—6:03 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>34. By a decree of which advance text is published today Portugal prohibits
                    exportation or transit of arms and munitions of war including <pb facs="0612"
                        n="513" xml:id="pg513"/> airplanes and ships to Spain. Decree to be
                    suspended in case enlistment or subscriptions of money are effected in signatory
                    countries.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caldwell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
